{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791128458,"nonce":"0PFsivRNaWdA5zTR2K8UoMkO50U=","message":"Follow-on from the ashui session: the measurers counted the gaps between\ncharacters, (n - 1) * letter_spacing, while blinc_text's layout advances\nby x_advance + letter_spacing after EVERY glyph, the last included. That\nis what CSS does, and it is why letter-spaced text looks shifted when\ncentred.\n\nNarrower than first reported, and worth recording because the report was\nnot quite right. All three (n - 1) sites were ESTIMATOR paths:\nEstimatedTextMeasurer's two in text_measure.rs and\nFontTextMeasurer::estimate_size in text_measurer.rs. With a real face\ninstalled, FontTextMeasurer delegates to TextLayoutEngine::layout, the\nsame code that draws, so the real path already counted every character.\nVerified rather than assumed, in\ncrates/blinc_layout/tests/letter_spacing_trailing.rs: measuring \"A\",\n\"AB\" and \"ABCD\" with and without spacing shows n spacings, not n - 1.\n\nSo the fix makes the fallback agree with the real path and the renderer,\nand it will NOT move numbers for any caller that installs a measurer.\nA residual half-spacing offset on a centred single glyph comes from\nwhole-pixel glyph positioning instead, which is what\nTextRenderer::prepare_text_subpixel exists for.\n\nThe estimator tests deliberately install no measurer and depend on\nnextest giving each test its own process; under cargo test a sibling\ncalling init_text_measurer would install the global first and they would\nsilently measure through the real path.\n\nAn earlier test of mine had encoded the (n - 1) convention and had to\nmove with it.\n\nFound next door and filed separately: word_spacing is added by both\nmeasurers and applied by blinc_text nowhere at all.","files":null}]}